  "result": "Done! I've added foreign currency support to the system. Here's what was added:\n\n**Added to src/money.js:**\n\n**RATES constant:**\n- EUR: 1 (base currency)\n- USD: 1.085 (units of USD per euro)\n- GBP: 0.8425 (units of GBP per euro)\n\n**convert(cents, currency)** \u2014 converts euro cents to target currency:\n- Input: euro cents, currency code\n- Output: ok(converted_cents) or fail(UNKNOWN_CURRENCY)\n- EUR to EUR returns same amount\n- Uses roundCents for banker's rounding (half to even)\n- Example: convert(10000, 'USD') \u2192 10850 cents (\u20ac100 = $108.50)\n\n**formatMoney(cents, currency)** \u2014 formats amounts with currency symbols:\n- Input: amount in target currency (cents), currency code\n- Output: formatted string with symbol, thousands separators, 2 decimals\n- EUR: \u20ac1,234.56\n- USD: $1,234.56\n- GBP: \u00a31,234.56\n- Handles negative amounts: -$123.45\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- UNKNOWN_CURRENCY error code\n\n**Created test/currency.test.js:**\n- 33 comprehensive test cases covering:\n  - RATES constant values\n  - Convert to each currency (EUR, USD, GBP)\n  - Unknown currency rejection\n  - Rounding examples\n  - Large amounts\n  - formatMoney with all currency symbols\n  - Thousands separators\n  - Negative amounts\n  - Padding and decimal consistency\n  - Convert + format chains\n\n**Results:**\n- All 279 tests passing (33 new currency tests + 21 CSV + 10 late fee + 15 VAT + 16 overdue + 184 existing)\n- Exchange rates fixed in code\n- Banker's rounding maintains precision\n- Consistent formatting across all currencies",
